# Force a text diff for source files regardless of what git's binary
# heuristic makes of their contents.
#
# stationTimes.ts used a raw NUL byte as a delimiter; SPA-245 replaced it with
# a unicode escape. One NUL is enough for git to call the whole file binary,
# which cost that file its diff on GitHub — the change was reviewed blind. A
# pre-image still holding the byte keeps a diff binary even once the post-image
# is clean, so the escape alone does not bring the diff back.
#
# These only affect how a diff is rendered: no filtering, no line-ending
# translation, nothing that touches what is stored or checked out.
*.ts diff
*.vue diff
